From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 999998: do not let an unmeasured link erase a measured throughput estimate

The exact twin of 99993 (keep measured rcpi), two lines above it: an MLO
client is reported once per affiliated link, an idle link has nothing to
estimate and honestly reports 0, all reports land on the single sta row
the MLD has, and both writers of dl_est_thput/ul_est_thput are
unconditional - so the measured estimate is routinely erased by an
unmeasured one, in the same callback whose rcpi we already guard.

The blind review of 2026-08-04 flagged this as finding 1.5 and the series
pattern it belongs to ("fixed one site out of N"). Both writer sites get
the same guard as rcpi:

  - the associated-STA link metrics path (next to the guarded rcpi), and
  - the per-BSS link-metrics-response path (next to the guarded ul_rcpi).

Zero-as-no-reading is the correct interpretation on both: the TLV carries
an estimate the AP computed, and an AP that measured nothing sends 0, not
an estimate of 0 - a link with a real estimate of zero throughput would be
a dead link, which association state reports separately.

Cost, as with rcpi: a client that leaves keeps its last estimate until the
row is released. Association state says whether the client is there; the
estimate says what the link could do while it was.

Verify on hardware: MLO client with one active link, watch
est_mac_rate_dl/ul in the sta table - with this patch they hold the
measured value instead of flapping to 0 with every idle-link report.
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -2518,8 +2518,14 @@
 
 		s = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table, p->macaddr);
 		if (s) {
-			s->de_sta->dl_est_thput = dl_est_thput;
-			s->de_sta->ul_est_thput = ul_est_thput;
+			/* Same single-row-per-MLD clobber as rcpi below: an idle
+			 * affiliated link estimates nothing and honestly reports 0,
+			 * and the last writer wins. A zero estimate never overwrites
+			 * a measured one - steering decisions divide by these. */
+			if (dl_est_thput)
+				s->de_sta->dl_est_thput = dl_est_thput;
+			if (ul_est_thput)
+				s->de_sta->ul_est_thput = ul_est_thput;
 			/* An MLO client is reported once per affiliated link, and a link
 			 * the client is not transmitting on has nothing to measure, so it
 			 * honestly sends rcpi 0. All those reports land on the one row this
@@ -3180,8 +3186,12 @@
 				continue;
 			}
 
-			s->de_sta->dl_est_thput = BUF_GET_BE32(b->dl_thput);
-			s->de_sta->ul_est_thput = BUF_GET_BE32(b->ul_thput);
+			/* Zero means the link measured nothing - same clobber and same
+			 * trade as ul_rcpi below, so the same guard. */
+			if (BUF_GET_BE32(b->dl_thput))
+				s->de_sta->dl_est_thput = BUF_GET_BE32(b->dl_thput);
+			if (BUF_GET_BE32(b->ul_thput))
+				s->de_sta->ul_est_thput = BUF_GET_BE32(b->ul_thput);
 			s->de_sta->time_delta = BUF_GET_BE32(b->time_delta);
 			/* record link-metrics-response receive time */
 			time(&s->de_sta->tsp);
